1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:04,840
-[THEODNEY] Name: Tsav.
-[TSAV] That's me!

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,050
No surname.

3
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:07,680
Known as the "Man-Eating Ghoul."

4
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:09,680
Yeah, that whole
codename business

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,390
is pretty typical for assassins
of the Gwen Mohsa.

6
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:14,720
[THEODNEY] You had
eight kills in one month.

7
00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:16,430
That's rather disturbing.

8
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:19,190
[TSAV] Nah, you've got
your facts twisted.

9
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:20,520
I'm honest to a fault,

10
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,230
so I'll let you in on something.

11
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:25,570
It was actually 12!
That's a lot more.

12
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:27,190
-[Theodney exclaims]
-You see,

13
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:30,030
I'm so darn truthful
I'm basically a pushover!

14
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:33,740
Guess that's why I'm always
drawin' the short straw.

15
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:35,830
[THEODNEY]
You killed all those people,

16
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:38,290
yet you feel no remorse
whatsoever?

17
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,330
Aw, shit, I'm sorry, man.

18
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:42,420
Is this one of those
"right and wrong" things?

19
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:45,710
I'm not great at all that
philosophical morality junk.

20
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:48,130
Although, it feels
sort of crappy

21
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:49,800
to have to kill someone I like,

22
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,720
but everything beyond that
is all right by me!

23
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:56,140
Oh, and none of the Gwen Mohsa
brainwashing really stuck.

24
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:59,270
It always seemed too ridiculous
to try and take seriously.

25
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,110
We are well aware
of how they operate.

26
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:06,820
They dispense pain,
drugs, pleasure.

27
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:08,780
Whatever they have to do
to turn children--

28
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:10,490
Oh! Are you tryin' to say

29
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,530
I'm some kind of
foretold chosen one?

30
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:16,160
I won't argue, but that's such
a big responsibility!

31
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,910
[chuckles]

32
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:19,870
-Have you no fear?
-Mm?

33
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:22,830
Unless you manage
to get a life sentence,

34
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,460
death awaits you.

35
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:26,380
Are you not afraid?

36
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:28,380
Shakin' in my boots,

37
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:31,680
but I know full well that
fear won't change a thing.

38
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:34,890
So, why not have a good time
while I can?

39
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:37,470
That is hardly
a normal reaction.

40
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:39,810
Can you not envision
your future?

41
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:41,020
[TSAV] Don't be cruel!

42
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,400
I'm envisioning the hell
out of all that!

43
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:45,060
Thing is...

44
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:47,440
I still can't wrap
my head around it.

45
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,230
I mean, aside from
whatever's good for me

46
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,780
-and the people I like...
-[exclaims]

47
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,570
...nothin' else really matters.

48
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,080
[Theodney breathes uneasily]

49
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:00,160
[Kafzen chuckles]

50
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:02,790
[KAFZEN] How very fascinating.

51
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:04,210
Tsav, was it?

52
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:05,790
What method do you employ

53
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:07,750
when selecting your next target?

54
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:08,880
Didn't have one.

55
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:11,800
Just shot whoever seemed
easy to kill.

56
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:14,470
Is that a fact?

57
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,930
What about the fellow
named Taldy?

58
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:20,310
He vanished from
the government office

59
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:21,600
where he worked,

60
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,850
in a mere seventy seconds
in broad daylight.

61
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,360
Was he "easy to kill?"

62
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:30,900
Technique or whatever
isn't really the hard part.

63
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,950
I doubt there's
anyone I couldn't kill

64
00:02:32,990 --> 00:02:34,700
if I set my mind to it.

65
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,950
See, when I say "easy,"

66
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:39,950
I mean folks I won't feel bad
about murdering.

67
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:43,460
And how exactly
do you determine that?

68
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,630
Well, I guess you can
chalk it up to gut instinct.

69
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:49,540
They just seemed
easy to kill, you know?

70
00:02:49,590 --> 00:02:52,590
[KAFZEN] Instinct. Yes, I see.

71
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,550
[KAFZEN] Magnificent.

72
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:02,890
Anyhow, it seems death
is too good for you.

73
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:04,100
[TSAV] Uh?

74
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:06,560
[Tsav breathes shakily]

75
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,730
[TSAV] A sentence
worse than death?

76
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:10,230
Correct.

77
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:12,480
You are sentenced to be a hero.

78
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:15,150
Please, no!
This can't be right!

79
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:16,400
That penalty--

80
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,660
But it is right.

81
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:20,780
[chuckles]

82
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:26,370
There will be no sweet release
of death for you.

83
00:03:26,670 --> 00:03:29,210
[♪ opening theme song playing]

84
00:04:56,670 --> 00:04:58,510
[birds chirping]

85
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,270
[TSAV] Don't you see?

86
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:13,270
I'm essentially a total pushover
when you think about it.

87
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,570
The more I look at a target,
the more I think,

88
00:05:15,610 --> 00:05:17,480
"Whoa, I can't kill this guy!

89
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:19,360
He's got a wife
and kiddos at home!"

90
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:21,610
I'm too nice for my own good.
So...

91
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:24,030
He's a rather unusual hero.

92
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:26,490
Numerous deaths
have failed to change him.

93
00:05:26,530 --> 00:05:28,910
I just wish he'd stop
repeating that story.

94
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:30,410
[TSAV] So I'd mess up
some other guy's face

95
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,370
and bring him back
with me instead.

96
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:33,920
-I'm a big softie--
-[XYLO] Tsav.

97
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,040
Enough already.

98
00:05:35,090 --> 00:05:37,340
[Tsav laughs]
Sorry 'bout that, bro!

99
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:39,800
Was I talkin'
your ear off again?

100
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,680
Can we please put a muzzle
on this guy already?

101
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,970
He's gonna keep us up all night

102
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,510
if we have to share
a room with him!

103
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:46,600
[TSAV] But I can't stand it

104
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:48,520
when it gets too quiet,
you know?

105
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,680
I'm traumatized!

106
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,020
'Cause I have
a woefully tragic past.

107
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,190
What, with all the torture

108
00:05:53,230 --> 00:05:54,600
that was part
of my assassin training,

109
00:05:54,650 --> 00:05:55,860
they'd toss me
in a dungeon and--

110
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,230
Be quiet.
That's your last warning.

111
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:00,070
You had to go
and make him angry.

112
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:02,490
Aw, shit! Sorry, bro!

113
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,780
Dotta, say you're sorry, too!

114
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:06,780
-[DOTTA] Huh? Why should I?
-[Xylo sighs]

115
00:06:06,830 --> 00:06:07,910
[DOTTA] This is why I hate you,

116
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,660
'cause you completely lack
perspective!

117
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,830
[TSAV] Now, now.

118
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:12,540
You've gotta learn
to take a joke, Dotta!

119
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,290
Stress is bad for your health.

120
00:06:16,170 --> 00:06:19,050
[monsters grunting]

121
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:24,090
[monster growls]

122
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:31,230
They're advancing swiftly.

123
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:32,350
At this rate,

124
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:34,690
they'll most likely arrive
by tonight.

125
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,360
[Kivia gasps]

126
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,270
[KIVIA] Um, agreed.

127
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:41,530
I almost hate to ask,

128
00:06:41,570 --> 00:06:43,650
but how many knights
are staying?

129
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,110
About fifty.

130
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:47,700
I would trust each one of them
with my life.

131
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,660
That's not nearly enough.

132
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:51,200
Even with the prisoners

133
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:53,250
Venetim rounded up
from Milnid Jail.

134
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:55,670
How'd he get them? Bribery?

135
00:06:55,710 --> 00:06:58,090
Of course,
"they're all on death row,

136
00:06:58,130 --> 00:06:59,840
so do whatever you want
with 'em."

137
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:03,340
[chuckles] The universal
treatment for prisoners.

138
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:06,050
Hey! Over there!
Looks like some faerie scouts.

139
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:07,760
No kidding.

140
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:09,140
Let me see.

141
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,640
Hmm...

142
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,110
It looks like an ugly dog.

143
00:07:19,150 --> 00:07:21,360
My bet, it's a cir sith.

144
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:23,400
He can see it from here?

145
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:26,360
The man's vision
is absolutely inhuman.

146
00:07:26,410 --> 00:07:27,950
Tsav, you got it?

147
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,280
I guess we'll soon find out.

148
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:31,910
Just one thing.

149
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:35,040
Swear you won't kill me
if I miss.

150
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:37,500
He has a Verkle Corp Daisy?

151
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,790
Better.

152
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:41,340
His Majesty tuned it
for long-range sniping.

153
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,590
Are you sure we wanna
go through with this?

154
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,090
If he's in a pack,
his buddies--

155
00:07:45,130 --> 00:07:47,630
-[XYLO] Shut up and shoot.
-[Tsav gasps]

156
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:48,930
[Tsav grunts]

157
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,510
If you say so.

158
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,110
I did it!

159
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:05,610
That's a bullseye, people!

160
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:07,280
More. Incoming.

161
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,410
-I'm on it.
-[shoots]

162
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,540
[KIVIA] Can we truly
trust them with this?

163
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,790
[XYLO] They're effective
as they are obnoxious.

164
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,120
They'll get it done.

165
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:20,420
Tsav, in particular,
has never missed a shot

166
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:21,960
as far as I'm aware.

167
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,210
Anyway, we had better go
and set the trap.

168
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:26,590
-[Kivia sighs]
-[DOTTA] Keep going,

169
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:28,930
-there are more.
-[XYLO] What's wrong?

170
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:31,680
You aren't giving up
even in this situation?

171
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,100
Someone wants us dead

172
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:35,770
and I don't intend
to give them the satisfaction.

173
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:37,230
Besides...

174
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:41,230
there's that nonsense
about her "usefulness."

175
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,320
-A little to the left...
-[KIVIA] I had heard you were

176
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,530
a ruthless man
who imperiled your unit

177
00:08:46,570 --> 00:08:48,360
in an attempt
to climb the ranks.

178
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:51,110
[chuckles] Which noble family
graced you

179
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,320
with a sense of humor?

180
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:53,910
I am not a noble.

181
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:55,490
That's unusual.

182
00:08:55,530 --> 00:08:57,120
Especially from Galtuile.

183
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:59,000
How is it that you're a captain?

184
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,960
-[DOTTA] Is that a faerie?
-[KIVIA] Hm...

185
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,750
One of the high priests
is my uncle.

186
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:09,050
Oh, so a top dog
at the Temple, no less.

187
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,050
That's why
I hadn't heard of you.

188
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:13,140
Bro, we're all done here!

189
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:15,430
Every last shot hit the target.

190
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:17,890
You two stay here
and keep watch.

191
00:09:17,930 --> 00:09:19,520
Let's go, Kivia.

192
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:23,360
-[birds squawking]
-[indistinct chatter]

193
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,730
[KNIGHT 1] Carry it inside!

194
00:09:24,770 --> 00:09:26,480
[KNIGHT 2] We need
more materials here!

195
00:09:26,530 --> 00:09:28,280
[KNIGHT 3]
The captain's ready to head out.

196
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,530
Hurry up!

197
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:45,710
[MAN] Captain Kivia,
must you stay?

198
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:48,260
It seems lowly
to watch heroes die.

199
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:50,510
But I will pray for your safety,

200
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,300
if I must.

201
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:57,970
I shall also be praying
for your well-being, Kivia.

202
00:09:58,310 --> 00:10:00,640
[MAN] Pelmerry,
stay close to me.

203
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,020
That man is a goddess killer.

204
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,270
[XYLO] Bastard.

205
00:10:04,310 --> 00:10:06,940
[PELMERRY] Thank you, Hord.
I will comply.

206
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,570
[Xylo grunts]

207
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:11,150
Tell me, for I wish to know.

208
00:10:11,190 --> 00:10:12,900
Was I useful in my role?

209
00:10:12,950 --> 00:10:15,870
You were perfect.
Utterly flawless.

210
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,830
I see.

211
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:22,290
Then will you say those words?
"Well done"?

212
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,000
If you insist.

213
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,130
Well done, Pelmerry.

214
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,380
[HORD] If you'll excuse us.

215
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:42,350
I take it that was
the ninth goddess?

216
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:44,770
Correct. The Goddess Pelmerry.

217
00:10:45,190 --> 00:10:47,310
She's pacted
with Hord Clivios,

218
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,980
captain of the Ninth Order.

219
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:50,280
Do you know him?

220
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,610
I know his family owns
a lot of land

221
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:54,110
and a vineyard in the south.

222
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:55,650
There are some people
who would kill

223
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:57,570
for a cask of their wine.

224
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,080
Although...

225
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:02,120
what's in there now
is far more bitter than sweet.

226
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:07,040
[TSAV] Whoa,
that looks dangerous!

227
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:10,000
So our big plan is to lure
the Demon Lord over here

228
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,630
and then detonate
these barrels?

229
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:13,300
[XYLO] Right,
we're killing Iblis

230
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,050
with an onslaught of poison.

231
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:17,430
That nasty poison's
gonna kill us too?

232
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:19,640
That completely sucks.

233
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:21,560
Pisses me off, to be honest.

234
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,180
Might even drive me
to kill someone!

235
00:11:24,230 --> 00:11:25,390
[MAN] What?

236
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:28,230
Say that again,
if you have the guts.

237
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,610
You looking for a fight?

238
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:30,820
[chuckles]

239
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:33,690
[man grunts]
All you heroes disgust me.

240
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:36,360
-Better watch your--
-[grunts] Zofflec!

241
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,450
[Zofflec grunts]

242
00:11:37,490 --> 00:11:38,530
Yeah, all right.

243
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:44,910
Why do you think
you have to kill someone?

244
00:11:44,950 --> 00:11:46,540
I gotta vent my anger.

245
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:48,670
You can't tell me you've
never kicked a rock

246
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:50,130
when you were fired up.

247
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,500
[XYLO] Human beings
aren't rocks.

248
00:11:52,550 --> 00:11:54,760
[TSAV] Whoa!
That's human exceptionalism!

249
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:57,430
Humans are just one part
of our big wide world!

250
00:11:57,470 --> 00:11:59,090
Not fair to give 'em
special treatment.

251
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:01,510
[TEORITTA] I have found you
at last, Xylo!

252
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,220
Hey, Goddess!

253
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:05,520
So did you like
holding down the fort?

254
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:07,770
Spare me your pleasantries!

255
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,600
Do you realize
that you callously left

256
00:12:09,650 --> 00:12:10,810
without telling me?

257
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:13,230
Such conduct is unbecoming
of my knight!

258
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:14,400
I can explain.

259
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:16,820
Honor demanded
that we fulfill our duty.

260
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:17,990
Have mercy.

261
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:19,360
[Teoritta grunts]

262
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:22,740
[Teoritta grunts]

263
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:25,790
Xylo,

264
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:29,500
did you perchance enjoy
scouting with Kivia?

265
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:32,380
There's no such thing
as enjoyable scouting.

266
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:34,340
Goddess Teoritta, have a look.

267
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,340
I found some nice berries
in the forest.

268
00:12:37,510 --> 00:12:39,470
They're ripe and sweet.

269
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:42,100
[Teoritta grunts]

270
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:43,640
Picking berries?

271
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,140
In the forest?

272
00:12:45,310 --> 00:12:46,730
Together?

273
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:49,060
That sounds rather delightful.

274
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:50,440
-It wasn't!
-Got a map?

275
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:51,810
-Sure do.
-Duty required that we gather

276
00:12:51,850 --> 00:12:52,860
supplies.

277
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:55,070
My knight, listen well!

278
00:12:55,110 --> 00:12:56,820
-I observed the Ninth Order...
-Here you go.

279
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,490
-...of the Holy Knights!
-Appreciate it.

280
00:12:58,530 --> 00:13:00,700
-Go on.
-[Teoritta grunts]

281
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:03,200
How dare you speak
so dismissively!

282
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,410
Listen carefully!

283
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:07,120
Their goddess received
head pats seven times!

284
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:08,710
She was praised
with seven separate pats

285
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:11,290
-within a single day!
-And what are you getting at?

286
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:14,590
I've not received even
one tiny head pat from you!

287
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:16,920
I do not expect
a generous seven pats,

288
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,220
but half would suffice! [grunts]

289
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,760
Yet despite my accomplishments,

290
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,680
I have not received
a single pat!

291
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,890
Hmph!

292
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:27,180
Noted.

293
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:29,100
-[Teoritta yells]
-[Tsav] Oh.

294
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:30,690
[TEORITTA] Fie!
Why do you fail to understand?

295
00:13:30,730 --> 00:13:33,100
I'm more concerned
about our lack of soldiers.

296
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:35,440
The faeries are going
to trample us

297
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,820
-if we don't do something.
-[TEORITTA] Pat my head!

298
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,030
[RAJIT] Captain Kivia,

299
00:13:38,070 --> 00:13:40,110
some strangers
arrived at the back gate.

300
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,570
They say they won't leave
until they see him.

301
00:13:43,450 --> 00:13:45,030
What about?

302
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,620
[insects trilling]

303
00:13:46,990 --> 00:13:48,540
[XYLO] You again?

304
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:49,870
[FOREMAN]
We caught wind

305
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:52,120
you were on
an impossible mission here.

306
00:13:52,170 --> 00:13:55,210
We're just some tired miners,
but we've gotta be worth

307
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:56,920
-somethin', right?
-[MEN] Yeah!

308
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:00,420
[Xylo sighs]

309
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,720
You do realize what we're
up against, don't you?

310
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:04,760
We want to help the king

311
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,720
and champions
who saved our lives,

312
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,850
same thing any man worth
his salt would do.

313
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:09,850
Hate to disappoint,

314
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:12,310
but we're not royals
or champions.

315
00:14:12,350 --> 00:14:14,350
Go back home to your families.

316
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,650
We're doing this for us as well.

317
00:14:17,110 --> 00:14:19,230
We all hail from these
surrounding villages

318
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,990
and we'll go back
when we're done.

319
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:23,360
We can't let what happened
in the mines

320
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,990
happen to the fortress, too.

321
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:28,410
It took our livelihoods,
but it can't have our homes.

322
00:14:30,790 --> 00:14:31,830
Look, I get it,

323
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:33,210
but you just
got your lives back

324
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:34,420
and you wanna
go and throw--

325
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:36,460
[NORGALLE]
My loyal subjects, welcome!

326
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,960
-[MINER] It's him!
-[NORGALLE] You're here at last!

327
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,710
The warriors of my realm!

328
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:42,170
You are the true heroes
of this day.

329
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:45,050
Majesty, don't encourage them.

330
00:14:45,090 --> 00:14:47,140
Why ever not, Commander Xylo?

331
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:50,180
Our forces are depleted,
and in need of brave men.

332
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:51,850
I'm aware, but still...

333
00:14:51,890 --> 00:14:53,980
-You know what'll happen.
-Of course.

334
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:56,350
I would never ask them
to throw their lives away,

335
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:59,230
but I refuse to balk
at a helping hand.

336
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:00,400
Huh?

337
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,940
I intend to take
these gallant soldiers

338
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:04,280
under my tutelage.

339
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,740
They'll soon be able to handle

340
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:08,070
even the most intricate
of sacred seal tuning.

341
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,280
[Xylo grunts]

342
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:12,040
[NORGALLE] Thanks to these
loyal servants of the crown,

343
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,370
the tides have turned!

344
00:15:13,410 --> 00:15:15,290
Together, we shall
make this fortress

345
00:15:15,330 --> 00:15:17,120
truly impregnable!

346
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:18,500
Trust me.

347
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:22,710
We shall snatch victory
from the jaws of defeat!

348
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:25,130
[ALL] Yes, Majesty!

349
00:15:25,630 --> 00:15:26,840
[NORGALLE] Follow me!

350
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:29,600
Our work demands
we begin at once!

351
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:31,770
[MINERS] Hail the king!
Hail the king!

352
00:15:31,810 --> 00:15:33,140
-Hail the king!
-[Xylo sighs]

353
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:35,890
Hail the king!
Hail the king! Hail the king!

354
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,610
[VENETIM] Not bad.

355
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:47,450
Seems everything's going
according to plan.

356
00:15:47,490 --> 00:15:49,660
By the way, Xylo,

357
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:51,870
what exactly is the plan?

358
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:53,160
[Xylo sighs]

359
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:56,120
Tatsuya seals
the underground passage.

360
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:58,710
I want 20 of the Order's knights
with him.

361
00:15:58,750 --> 00:15:59,830
[Tatsuya grunts]

362
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,670
[XYLO]
Tsav takes the back gate.

363
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,380
Shoot anyone who comes close.

364
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,050
[TSAV] Oh! My specialty!

365
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,510
[TSAV]
Hold on, where's Dotta?

366
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,760
He has his own mission
to complete.

367
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:12,810
The miners, they'll guard
the rear by the front gate.

368
00:16:12,850 --> 00:16:15,480
I want them backing up
the Knights.

369
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,940
We've been ordered not to raise
the drawbridge,

370
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:19,020
so it's dangerous.

371
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:20,650
Don't push it,

372
00:16:20,690 --> 00:16:22,770
but try to hold
for half the day.

373
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:25,440
[NORGALLE] We'll work
on tuning the sacred seals.

374
00:16:25,490 --> 00:16:28,200
Hey, Xylo, what are you
planning to do?

375
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:31,200
Attack it.

376
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:33,030
[ALL] Uh...

377
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,700
[all laugh]

378
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:37,460
-That's my bro for you.
-[NORGALLE] Hm.

379
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,920
Listen up.

380
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:42,000
Weather the faeries' advance
for as long as you can,

381
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,750
that should draw out Iblis.

382
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:46,340
Before it can make it
to the fortress,

383
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:49,510
I'll use a trap
we set in advance...

384
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,300
killing it.

385
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:53,850
That's the only way
we all live.

386
00:16:53,890 --> 00:16:55,470
Our last hope.

387
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:57,930
[PRISONER 1]
Ugh, give me a damn break!

388
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,100
[PRISONER 2] I'll kill you!

389
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,440
[PRISONER 3]
Don't tell us what to do!

390
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,020
[spits]

391
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:04,730
Why should we follow the orders
of a pathetic hero like you?

392
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:07,280
Well, you people are subhuman,

393
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:10,030
and you're nothing but
a goddess-killing bastard--

394
00:17:10,950 --> 00:17:13,280
-Uh?
-[prisoner screaming]

395
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:14,660
[screaming continues]

396
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:19,160
[TSAV] Can you stop trying
to piss off my bro?

397
00:17:19,210 --> 00:17:22,000
'Cause I'm not in the mood
to deal with the blowback.

398
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:24,750
But why didn't you
shoot me instead?

399
00:17:24,790 --> 00:17:26,420
[TSAV] You wanna know why?

400
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:29,800
It's because you're a lot bigger
and stronger than that guy is.

401
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,050
So you'll be much more
useful to us. [chuckles]

402
00:17:32,090 --> 00:17:33,590
[prisoner crying]

403
00:17:34,350 --> 00:17:35,510
[TSAV] Uh?

404
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:38,220
[Tsav grunts]

405
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:39,430
[Tsav choking]

406
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:43,190
[XYLO] Tsav, that was
extremely effective,

407
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:45,980
but don't do it again.

408
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:47,610
[Tsav coughing]

409
00:17:48,990 --> 00:17:50,400
[breathes deeply]

410
00:17:50,950 --> 00:17:52,990
Oh, now I get it!
I should've killed him--

411
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,450
-[Tsav screams, grunts]
-[XYLO] Wrong answer.

412
00:17:55,490 --> 00:17:58,200
Go use a sacred seal
to stem his bleeding.

413
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,000
[all exclaiming]

414
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:05,590
[birds chirping]

415
00:18:07,090 --> 00:18:09,010
[XYLO] Well, what do you want?

416
00:18:09,050 --> 00:18:12,220
A sealed letter has arrived
addressed to you, Xylo.

417
00:18:12,630 --> 00:18:13,680
Seems it's from--

418
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:16,220
Burn it. I'm not reading it.

419
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,600
[VENETIM] Uh...

420
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:20,100
Um, sure, although you might be
interested to know

421
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,230
that it's from
Frenci Mastibolt.

422
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:24,400
I assume you've heard
of the Mastibolts.

423
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,560
A family of night-gaunts
from the south.

424
00:18:26,610 --> 00:18:29,190
They want to lend us
some soldiers.

425
00:18:29,230 --> 00:18:31,650
It's a rather generous offer,

426
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:35,620
and we're in desperate need
of extra manpower, right?

427
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:37,370
Don't you think--

428
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:40,790
-[whimpers]
-This conversation's over.

429
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:43,870
I won't mention it again.

430
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,290
Even though we could really use
2,000 soldiers.

431
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:48,420
[XYLO] Moving on.

432
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,760
Why aren't Jayce
and Rhyno here yet?

433
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:53,800
[VENETIM] Jayce replied that
he refuses to overwork Neely,

434
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,720
then threatened to kill me.

435
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,850
And Rhyno ignored my message.

436
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:01,560
I should know to expect that
from a volunteer hero.

437
00:19:01,770 --> 00:19:03,480
And the mercenaries?

438
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:05,520
I tried contacting them,

439
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,020
but since we can't pay...

440
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:09,020
Dotta's out raising money.

441
00:19:09,070 --> 00:19:11,400
Just hope he's back in time.

442
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:14,900
[NORGALLE] Greetings!
Good morrow, soldiers!

443
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:16,530
-Be careful and haul it in.
-[Xylo sighs]

444
00:19:16,570 --> 00:19:18,910
[XYLO] We need to
keep them off the front line.

445
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,580
It'll be the end of days
before I make them fight.

446
00:19:23,450 --> 00:19:25,580
[VENETIM] The end of days.

447
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:28,040
[MINER] Your Majesty,
what do you want us to do next?

448
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:30,170
[VENETIM]
Xylo, I've got a little

449
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:32,710
-thought experiment for you.
-[MINER] Right!

450
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,430
What if there really
are people plotting

451
00:19:36,470 --> 00:19:38,300
to put an end to humanity?

452
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:40,050
What would you do?

453
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:47,390
-Why ask?
-[objects clattering]

454
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,770
[VENETIM] Do you believe them?

455
00:19:48,810 --> 00:19:50,360
Conspiracy theories?

456
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,530
[Xylo scoffs]
This is pointless.

457
00:19:52,570 --> 00:19:54,650
I'm already aware
of those bullshit articles

458
00:19:54,690 --> 00:19:57,070
you used to write
about Demon Lord worshippers

459
00:19:57,110 --> 00:19:59,200
and coexistence advocates.

460
00:19:59,570 --> 00:20:01,740
You clearly made
the whole thing up.

461
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:02,990
[VENETIM] I suppose

462
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:05,410
I can't really blame you
for thinking that.

463
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:10,170
But say there is a faction
worshiping Demon Lords

464
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:12,130
or seeking coexistence
with them,

465
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:16,260
and taking steps to ensure
humanity loses the fight...

466
00:20:16,970 --> 00:20:20,090
Wouldn't it explain
a lot of things, like...

467
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:23,140
this nonsensical mission
we're on?

468
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,470
♪

469
00:20:26,810 --> 00:20:29,520
If those people truly existed,

470
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:33,270
they'd have to be
the shittiest scumbags ever.

471
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:40,530
[monsters growling]

472
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,330
[Xylo grunts]
Iblis is still far away.

473
00:20:51,630 --> 00:20:53,670
[Teoritta gasps]
They have arrived, my knight.

474
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:56,170
-[horses neighing]
-[XYLO] Coiste bodhars.

475
00:20:56,210 --> 00:20:58,170
The vanguard of the horde.

476
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,260
Here we go.

477
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,180
It begins now.

478
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,850
[horses neighing]

479
00:21:04,890 --> 00:21:06,260
♪

480
00:21:06,310 --> 00:21:08,230
[NORGALLE] The future
of humanity depends

481
00:21:08,270 --> 00:21:09,770
upon today's battle.

482
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:12,190
We must protect our homeland!

483
00:21:12,770 --> 00:21:14,310
Hold. Men, set!

484
00:21:16,530 --> 00:21:17,650
His Majesty.

485
00:21:17,690 --> 00:21:20,400
I told him to stay
in the back, dammit.

486
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:22,320
Get ready.

487
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:23,700
Fire!

488
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:27,080
[screeching]

489
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:35,340
[MINER 1]
Activate the barricades!

490
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:36,460
[MINER 2] On it!

491
00:21:51,940 --> 00:21:53,900
[NORGALLE]
Another job well done.

492
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:56,480
Your noble efforts
gave us a leg up!

493
00:21:56,820 --> 00:21:58,940
[miners cheering]

494
00:21:58,990 --> 00:22:01,240
Now prepare the next volley!

495
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:02,660
Ungood.

496
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:04,950
His Majesty's by the front line.

497
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:09,040
Hey, Venetim! If somethin'
happens to the king,

498
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:11,000
-we're all doomed, right?
-They're here! Fire!

499
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:13,790
[VENETIM] I tried my best
to talk him out of it,

500
00:22:13,830 --> 00:22:15,710
but he wouldn't listen
to reason.

501
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:19,050
[TSAV] If you can't talk people
outta doin' stupid stuff,

502
00:22:19,090 --> 00:22:20,670
then what good are you?

503
00:22:21,220 --> 00:22:22,880
[VENETIM] Well,
that's an exceptionally

504
00:22:22,930 --> 00:22:24,010
rude thing to say.

505
00:22:24,050 --> 00:22:25,010
[laughs]

506
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:27,180
[SIENA] The cavalry is here!

507
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:29,470
We must support Captain Kivia!

508
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,890
Fire!

509
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:36,020
[KIVIA] Onward! Now,
Thirteenth Order.

510
00:22:36,230 --> 00:22:38,190
Let the battle begin!

511
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:41,400
[all yelling]

512
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,530
[Kivia yells]

513
00:22:48,830 --> 00:22:49,950
[Kivia grunts]

514
00:22:53,460 --> 00:22:55,330
[all yelling]

515
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:04,130
[KIVIA] Zofflec!

516
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:05,970
Cavalry, hurry!

517
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:07,590
Turn back!

518
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:09,890
Keep harrying them!

519
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:12,350
If they get in the fortress,
it's over!

520
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,600
[TEORITTA] Wow.

521
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:16,310
Their valiant efforts
are rather impressive.

522
00:23:17,190 --> 00:23:18,360
[TSAV] Hey, bro!

523
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:20,730
What's over there?

524
00:23:20,770 --> 00:23:21,940
[TEORITTA] Uh?

525
00:23:22,110 --> 00:23:23,110
[Xylo gasps]

526
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:25,400
[TSAV] Isn't that...

527
00:23:25,910 --> 00:23:28,780
[XYLO] Yeah,
I can see them, too.

528
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:31,330
-[horse neighs]
-[KIVIA] Huh?

529
00:23:34,450 --> 00:23:36,580
[XYLO]
But I still can't believe it.

530
00:23:37,750 --> 00:23:39,340
[ALL] Humans?

531
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:44,010
[MINER 1] Flaming arrows?

532
00:23:44,050 --> 00:23:46,050
[MINER 2]
The barricade's on fire!

533
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:47,970
We're in trouble.

534
00:23:48,010 --> 00:23:49,600
[MINER 3]
The sacred seals are ruined!

535
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:50,760
What now?

536
00:23:50,930 --> 00:23:52,680
[MINER 4] Don't let
the barrels catch fire!

537
00:23:56,940 --> 00:23:58,350
[KNIGHT 1] Second wave incoming!

538
00:23:58,400 --> 00:23:59,650
[KNIGHT 2]
We're grossly outnumbered!

539
00:23:59,690 --> 00:24:01,610
We can't stop that many!

540
00:24:01,650 --> 00:24:03,030
Dammit.

541
00:24:03,070 --> 00:24:05,320
[MINER] The portcullis on
the front gate won't hold!

542
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:06,950
They're gonna break through!

543
00:24:06,990 --> 00:24:08,950
-[distant yelling]
-[neighing]

544
00:24:09,370 --> 00:24:10,950
If this keeps up,

545
00:24:10,990 --> 00:24:14,750
before that damn Demon Lord
even makes it to the fortress...

546
00:24:14,790 --> 00:24:16,450
[miner whimpering]

547
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,420
-[miner screams]
-[squelching]

548
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,340
[neighs]

549
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:26,380
[XYLO]...everyone here
will already be dead.
